@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Health - Mongo
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health/mongo

### Create Post (example)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/post
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderId": "user1",
  "title": "Welcome to Colman API",
  "content": "This is an example post created via rest.rest"
}

### List Posts (all)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/post

### List Posts (filter by sender)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/post?sender=user1

### Get Post by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/post/{{postId}}

### Update Post (partial update payload example)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/post/{{postId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated title",
  "content": "Updated content"
}

### Create Comment (example)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/comment
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "postId": "{{postId}}",
  "senderId": "user2",
  "content": "Nice post! Thanks for sharing."
}

### Get Comment by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/comment/{{commentId}}

### Update Comment
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/comment/{{commentId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Edited comment content"
}

### Delete Comment
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comment/{{commentId}}

### Get Comments For Post
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/post/{{postId}}/comments

### Helpful notes
# - Replace `{{postId}}` and `{{commentId}}` with IDs returned from create requests.
# - This REST client file intentionally omits Authorization headers so it works against an unauthenticated JSON DAL or dev server.

